<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Oromo (Afaan Oromoo, in Qubee), a draft not yet read by a fluent reviewer (#495). The notes on each string are in values/strings.xml.
    The app speaks to the driver as "ati" (Seeni, Filadhu, kee), as Oromo phone menus do.
    "Vehicle" is konkolaataa, never the word for bus; "route" is daandii; "run" is marsaa (a round); "trip" is imala;
    "stop" is buufata; "block" is bilookii; "report" is gabaasa (plural gabaasota); "dispatcher" is to'ataa;
    "agency" is dhaabbata; "riders" are imaltoota; "server" is sarvarii; "connection" is interneetii;
    "location" is bakka; "settings" is qindaa'ina; "diagnostics" is odeeffannoo appii.
    Android has no Oromo screens, so the permission rows use plain Oromo words. "min" and "h" are written in full
    (daqiiqaa, sa'aatii).
-->
